{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The geometry sweep is stable enough to commit: small tensors prefer wider per-row tiles, mid-sized tensors prefer one wave per 128 elements, and the largest tensors gain slightly by pairing two rows per workgroup. These are only launch-layout choices—the same fused arithmetic runs for every element. I’m cleaning out the experimental math paths now and will use verification attempt 3 on the tuned dispatcher."}}
